DPDK 25.11.3 ENA PMD changes for conduit (applied by docker/Dockerfile).
- read_clock: the device PHC (ns) through rte_eth_read_clock; PHC set up at device init and
  destroyed at close, so rte_eth_dev_reset frees and rebuilds it.
- ena_timer_wd_callback: when trigger_reset is already set (a datapath fault: bad TX/RX
  req_id, malformed RX descriptor, TX prepare-context error), raise RTE_ETH_EVENT_INTR_RESET
  instead of returning early, so the application learns of it and calls rte_eth_dev_reset.
  Stock code returns early and never reports those faults.
- xstats: propagate customer and legacy metrics query failures and reject incomplete customer
  metrics support rather than exposing unsupported counters as valid values.

